<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Destruction Warlocks</span></h3>
<i>Most</i> crafted gear is no longer profession-locked, so you can equip Tailoring pieces freely. While weaker than mid-Phase 3 gear, several crafted items can help jumpstart your gearing process.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94278/falling-blossom-cowl">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Cowl" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_cloth_raidmage_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Cowl</span></a> is a strong crafted helm option for Warlocks, featuring valuable secondary stats with both Hit and Mastery. The high base Intellect and Stamina make it a durable and well-rounded choice before obtaining raid gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94277/falling-blossom-treads">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_cloth_raidmage_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Treads</span></a> is a solid crafted option for  Warlocks, offering a combination of Hit and Mastery. With two Red sockets and a Mastery socket bonus, they provide excellent gemming flexibility to boost key stats further.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82437/spelltwisters-grand-robe">
<img alt="Spelltwister's Grand Robe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_robe_raidmage_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spelltwister's Grand Robe</span></a> has excellent stats for Destruction Warlock, offering plenty of Haste and Mastery. Also, due to its higher item level, it helps you queue into Heroic and Celestial Dungeons faster.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82438/spelltwisters-gloves">
<img alt="Spelltwister's Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_raidmage_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spelltwister's Gloves</span></a> has plenty of Hit. This is welcome, since it allows you to reach the Hit Cap more easily. The same is true with the chest piece from this set. It also increases your item level a fair bit early on, allowing you to queue into Heroic and Celestial dungeons faster.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77533/lightweight-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Lightweight Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweight Retinal Armor</span></a> from Engineering allows you to pick the secondary stats you want using Tinker's Gears, such as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77545/rigid-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Rigid Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Tinker's Gear</span></a>. Its item level is quite high, considering the point in the game you can get it. This makes it a strong, early-crafted option. <b>Note</b>: Requires Engineering.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79334/inscribed-jade-fan">
<img alt="Inscribed Jade Fan" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_1h_pandariatradeskill_c_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Jade Fan</span></a> originates from Inscription, but you can obtain it from other players or through the Auction House. Not powerful on its own, but it enables stronger main-hand + off-hand combos over staves.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Destruction Warlock Trinkets</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>While the specific type of trinket (active vs. passive) isn't overly critical for Warlocks, passive trinkets are inherently easier to use and maintain uptime on, making them ideal for players who may forget to use actives or have inconsistent cooldown alignment.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95669/wushoolays-final-choice">
<img alt="Wushoolay's Final Choice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_chainlightning.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wushoolay's Final Choice</span></a> is our best-in-slot Phase 3 trinket. It offers a large amount of Hit rating and a powerful Intellect proc that stacks.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95814/unerring-vision-of-lei-shen">
<img alt="Unerring Vision of Lei Shen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_hunter_focusedaim.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unerring Vision of Lei Shen</span></a> is an excellent trinket option thanks to its powerful proc, granting 100% Critical Strike Chance for 4 seconds. It also provides a large amount of passive Intellect.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95772/cha-yes-essence-of-brilliance">
<img alt="Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_mindsooth.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance</span></a> is one of the strongest pre-Siege trinkets available, providing Critical Strike as its passive and a powerful Intellect proc. With a proc rate scaling with your Critical Strike chance, it offers high uptime and excellent synergy for classes that naturally stack Crit.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81263/flashfrozen-resin-globule">
<img alt="Flashfrozen Resin Globule" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashfrozen Resin Globule</span></a> provides some much-needed Hit initially while still gearing up your character, allowing for more offensive secondary stats on the rest of your gear without worrying as much about getting to the Hit Cap. It's also very easy to obtain through basic Heroic dungeons.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89081/blossom-of-pure-snow">
<img alt="Blossom of Pure Snow" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_herbd.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blossom of Pure Snow</span></a> is available through the Shado-Pan reputation vendor, and is a great option if you haven't been able to obtain the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81263/flashfrozen-resin-globule">
<img alt="Flashfrozen Resin Globule" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashfrozen Resin Globule</span></a> and have plenty of Valor to spend. Otherwise, there is not much value in it, since it performs about the same as the Heroic dungeon option.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit Cap for Destruction Warlocks</span></h2>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>In Mists of Pandaria, spellcasters require <b>15% Spell Hit</b> to ensure their spells do not miss raid bosses. This means your abilities (like <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=29722/incinerate">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_burnout.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Incinerate</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=348/immolate">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_immolation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Immolate</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=116858/chaos-bolt">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warlock_chaosbolt.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chaos Bolt</span></a>, etc.) will always land once this cap is reached.<br/>
<br/>At level 90, this 15% Hit corresponds to approximately <b>5100 Hit Rating</b>. Note that this is slightly less for Humans and Gnomes if they use their respective racial weapons.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>For spellcasters in MoP, <b>Expertise also contributes to your Spell Hit chance</b>, up to the same 15% cap. This was a change introduced in Patch 5.0.4 to allow hybrid classes and specific gear setups to use Expertise as a viable stat for casters. Note that this also means that on items with Hit Rating, you can reforge another secondary stat to Expertise, increasing your total Hit Chance on items that already have the stat present.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Expertise and Hit Rating are interchangeable up to the 15% total Spell Hit cap</b>. After that, any excess in either stat provides no benefit.<br/>
<br/>This also means gear with Expertise can be valuable to a caster until you're capped, especially useful in early gearing or PvP gear sets.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Destruction Warlocks</span></h3>Warlocks will often ignore socket colors if the bonus isn't strong enough. In general, we prefer to use red <b>Intellect</b> gems, unless there's a compelling reason not to.<br/>
<br/>A good rule of thumb: <b>If the socket bonus is less than 20 Intellect or 30 of any rating stat</b>, it's often better to ignore the bonus and socket the strongest gem instead. That said, this depends on your current gear and stat balance. You should simulate your character to determine the optimal gemming strategy.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Socket</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95347/sinister-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Sinister Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sinister Primal Diamond</span></a> &gt; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76885/burning-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Burning Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Burning Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Socket</span>: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=83150/brilliant-serpents-eye">
<img alt="Brilliant Serpent's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Serpent's Eye</span></a> &gt; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76694/brilliant-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c7">Blue Socket</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76682/veiled-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Veiled Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Veiled Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c4">Yellow Socket</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76668/reckless-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Reckless Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reckless Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li></ul>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<hr/>Our Destruction Warlock guides are always updated with the latest information from in-game experience, simulations, and logs; make sure to check our changelog to this page by clicking on <b>View Changelog</b> at the top of the page.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
